[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186157437 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-12b67edd-e409-5ea0-9859-9fa94b363ebb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-12b67edd-e409-5ea0-9859-9fa94b363ebb" :question/id #uuid "12b67edd-e409-5ea0-9859-9fa94b363ebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-88457" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}{e}^{3x}-4x{e}^{3x}-12{e}^{3x}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}-4x{e}^{3x}-12{e}^{3x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x-12){e}^{3x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x-12=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-4x-12=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,6.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{3x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{3x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,6,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 6=-12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7de9c953-9396-5e7b-9be9-017863373246"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7de9c953-9396-5e7b-9be9-017863373246" :answer-field/id #uuid "7de9c953-9396-5e7b-9be9-017863373246" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-660eda51-d232-5b88-9bd1-a2c03b96321a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-660eda51-d232-5b88-9bd1-a2c03b96321a" "answer-61b10d9f-a72c-52f5-9148-9af198ae4115" "answer-44378ce2-6b6d-50f9-8219-f673e5079ada" "answer-cb9d3203-fb35-582c-af0f-5edb1642fe68" "answer-605ed3c1-ae12-54a3-81f7-60de52284930"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-660eda51-d232-5b88-9bd1-a2c03b96321a" :answer/id #uuid "660eda51-d232-5b88-9bd1-a2c03b96321a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61b10d9f-a72c-52f5-9148-9af198ae4115" :answer/id #uuid "61b10d9f-a72c-52f5-9148-9af198ae4115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44378ce2-6b6d-50f9-8219-f673e5079ada" :answer/id #uuid "44378ce2-6b6d-50f9-8219-f673e5079ada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb9d3203-fb35-582c-af0f-5edb1642fe68" :answer/id #uuid "cb9d3203-fb35-582c-af0f-5edb1642fe68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-605ed3c1-ae12-54a3-81f7-60de52284930" :answer/id #uuid "605ed3c1-ae12-54a3-81f7-60de52284930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157438 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" "question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/id #uuid "e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/math-academy-id "q-100794" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}=11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x} & =11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-11x\\cdot {5}^{x}-4\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-11x-4)\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4.$\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4,$ and their product is $(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 4=-\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d952e124-7588-56a7-81b3-154bceef8a55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" "answer-d6757daa-1d29-5c10-947c-afd176f4f5d9" "answer-6ea8cba7-d03a-516f-a0c3-30fb8354dfdd" "answer-86253246-2caa-5e0b-abae-547f561590f3" "answer-d952e124-7588-56a7-81b3-154bceef8a55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" :answer/id #uuid "98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6757daa-1d29-5c10-947c-afd176f4f5d9" :answer/id #uuid "d6757daa-1d29-5c10-947c-afd176f4f5d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ea8cba7-d03a-516f-a0c3-30fb8354dfdd" :answer/id #uuid "6ea8cba7-d03a-516f-a0c3-30fb8354dfdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86253246-2caa-5e0b-abae-547f561590f3" :answer/id #uuid "86253246-2caa-5e0b-abae-547f561590f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d952e124-7588-56a7-81b3-154bceef8a55" :answer/id #uuid "d952e124-7588-56a7-81b3-154bceef8a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/id #uuid "3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-100799" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}=36{e}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{e}^{x} & =36{e}^{x} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}-36{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-36){e}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-36=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-36=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+6)(3x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,2.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,2,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 2=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-459604d3-c555-5e7f-b4d3-0ad596a161eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-459604d3-c555-5e7f-b4d3-0ad596a161eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "459604d3-c555-5e7f-b4d3-0ad596a161eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" "answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" "answer-adcaa9ff-45f7-5db6-b2e3-d82e71396783" "answer-d2eb82f2-a647-5584-afd7-3c3b5045b584" "answer-beb695a1-1361-556b-b4fb-bedb79dc1f93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" :answer/id #uuid "4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer/id #uuid "ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer