fields "answer-field-7de9c953-9396-5e7b-9be9-017863373246"] [17592186157437 :knowledge-point/questions "question-12b67edd-e409-5ea0-9859-9fa94b363ebb"] ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/id #uuid "e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f"] ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/math-academy-id "q-100794"] ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}=11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x}?$"] ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x} & =11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-11x\\cdot {5}^{x}-4\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-11x-4)\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4.$\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4,$ and their product is $(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 4=-\\frac{4}{3}.$"] ["question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952"] ["answer-98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" :answer/id #uuid "98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9"] ["answer-98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-98428f30-5194-58f2-b856-5fc56747aac9" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-d6757daa-1d29-5c10-947c-afd176f4f5d9" :answer/id #uuid "d67