-f0d944a99952"] [17592186157438 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f"] ["question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/id #uuid "3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa"] ["question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-100799"] ["question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}=36{e}^{x}?$"] ["question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{e}^{x} & =36{e}^{x} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}-36{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-36){e}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-36=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-36=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+6)(3x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,2.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,2,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 2=-4.$"] ["question-3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-459604d3-c555-5e7f-b4d3-0ad596a161eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "459604d3-c555-5e7f-b4d3-0ad596a161eb"] ["answer-4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" :answer/id #uuid "4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26"] ["answer-4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4c7135a8-799d-5ef5-9d3d-470881e76d26" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer/id #uuid "ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf"] ["answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ea325e7e-7c0b-5864-bded-5700ce421acf" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-adcaa9ff-45f7-5